 may not be justified because they  no longer have that  shield from the legal system shireen  that allows them  to i hate to say it but  the old cliche shoot first and ask  questions later  because that's what they do right i mean  we've heard that term all our lives is  kind of an over the top hyperbole  but with qualified immunity that's what  they're allowed to do  because they don't get called out they  don't get questioned they don't get  placed in civil or criminal jeopardy  because the law is slanted in a way that  allows them  to use lethal force in situations where  you know a calm rational consideration  the facts  may make lethal force not justified and  for the ravens  to pivot from words to action with  specific  things that need to be done that's where  this movement needs to go it can't just  be  we're upset it has to be we're upset and  here's what needs to happen absolutely  this is bigger than a hashtag  and and that's kind of what everyone has  said it's got to be more than words it's  got to be more than statements and  the ravens hey if you want to know uh  what they want done here it is they  absolutely laid it out and if you saw on  on  twitter last night after they put that  out i mean it was one praise after  another praise and i'm sure there was  some in there that  had people upset but everything i saw  was oh my goodness if you want to see  action here's the action and and they  called for and they laid it out and they  said here it is this is what we need to  do to make this better  to move on to to find to end racism and  find some  social justice and they just laid it out  there and it was fantastic and and  hopefully it leads  to something but it's not just words  it's not just words on a paper they  offered something and i i i just thought  it was great  and you know they say the nfl is a  copycat league right  hey every other team every other team  take that statement and as as  sims would say to me copy paste copy  paste  just take that statement and put your  name on top of it the ravens are not  going to be upset  right if every team and wouldn't that be  great  if today every other team  just took that statement and issued that  same statement that would be powerful so  to the extent any of the other teams are  out there listening today  uh go ahead and do it and what are the  ravens going to complain  no they want these actions to happen and  the more people who stand up and call  for those actions  the actions become more likely to happen  one of the actions  that happened in pittsburgh was practice  went forward  and mike tomlin who's been the coach of  that team since 2007 he can read the  room like no other coach can read the  room  he decided to go forward he said they  didn't even consider not practicing  here's some of what tomlin had to say  uh we desire to have an impact and and  more so than statements and we want to  be proactive  in our behavior and our thoughts and so  we had continued conversations not  necessarily in reaction to  to the most recent events that have  transpired  um i i continue to appreciate the hearts  and spirits  of our players in terms of wanting to  participate and get  engaged in a positive way and express  themselves uh that  is their right um like i've said many  times they'll continue to be supported  by us  as long as their efforts are done so  thoughtfully and with class  and and so um i'm excited about  continuing to grow in that area as  is our football team and have an  understanding of our platform  and um and utilize it in a very positive  and constructive way but also understand  um that we're targets and our  perspectives and our opinions can be  weaponized for  agendas or against us and so we we  we want to move forward thoughtfully  with everything that we do  like we've mentioned uh we're excited  about being part of solutions if we can  be  it really is a sad commentary that  anyone who  believes that change needs to come in  this area  needs to be fearful that anything they  say  will somehow be used against them right  so it if you if you and look we we dealt  with this yesterday we're dealing with  it today my  email box was flooded with equal parts  praise and equal parts condemnation  for using this platform to bring light  to these issues and to  and to try to affect change but you know  that's something that  everyone in this arena is going to deal  with shireen any action you take  anything that you say  is potentially going to boomerang back  on you thrown at you by  by those who who just don't believe  don't agree  and don't see the need for change  yeah i found it interesting you know  there's four minority coaches in the nfl  and two did not practice yesterday  chose not to anthony lynn and ron rivera  the dolphins were off who have brian  flores as their head coach and  mike tomlin chose to to hold practice  and he does read the room as well as any  head coach in the nfl which is why he's  held his job as long as he has  and so this is an example of one size  doesn't fit all  every team is different ben  roethlisberger said this team didn't  take a vote but they did talk about it  and they talked about a lot and i know  every team in the nfl i guarantee you  i don't know it for a fact but i  guarantee you all 30 teams yesterday had  some sort of conversation  about these issues whether they  practiced or didn't practice  uh and and the steelers were one of  those teams that chose to practice and  are going to try to take it out  into the streets and do it in their  communities and find solutions and  and uh yeah you know mike tomlin he's  been great he's done a good job at it  and he'll continue to but he read his  room and he read his room as that team  needed to practice yesterday  there's one specific voice in the nfl  who is quickly building up the kind of  equity that insulates him from criticism  and he has a way of using the platform  that is not in any way threatening or  hostile it's very matter of fact and  it's patrick mahomes and he's made it  clear  that he's going to continue to use the  platform  for good here's some of what mahomes had  to say yesterday  they've done a good job of kind of  bringing in different people to talk to  us about social injustices and  then i think uh we've done a good job  amongst each other  of just getting each other's perspective  uh talking if  that's at lunch or if that's just in any  free time that we have because it is  it is something that's that's critical  in our in our country is how to find a  way to be better  and uh with the jacob blake shooting i  mean it's it's just  being transferred talking about it's  just crazy man that this is still going  on in the world that we live in today  and we're going to try to set the  example in whatever way possible  uh to show that we can get along and we  can really respect one another for who  they are  and not the color of their skin and  we're hoping that just that we can get  over this i mean  it's too long too long it's been too  long and we're going to try to get over  this and and get to where we all treat  each other  equally patrick toward that end you  became a voice in the social justice  movement  this off season what inspired you to do  so  like i said it's just been too long i  mean it's it's too much suffering it's  too much  uh people being treated differently and  i think i was just tired of it  i think everybody's been is tired of it  and it continues to happen and we have  to find a way to change  and i'm gonna be a voice i'm gonna do  whatever active whatever i can to  to make sure that we change and we can  make the world a better place and  whatever that takes uh travis is right  along with me we're gonna make sure that  we do  whatever it takes to put the world in a  better place yeah i think coach said it  best man everybody just got to love each  other and appreciate  uh one another for who they are their  differences  knowing